{"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"static","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"kirnbergerIII","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"WellTemperament","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/WellTemperament","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning15WellTemperamentV"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Four fifths — C→G, G→D, D→A, and A→E — are each narrowed by ¼ of the syntonic","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"comma, equal to ⁴√5 ≈ 696.578 cents. One fifth — F♯→C♯ — is narrowed by one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schisma (32805:32768), equal to 16384:10935 ≈ 699.977 cents. The remaining seven","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"fifths are pure (3:2). The circle closes exactly because one syntonic comma times","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"one schisma equals one Pythagorean comma.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The four quarter-comma fifths make C–E a pure major third (5:4). Published in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Die Kunst des reinen Satzes in der Musik"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", Part II.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/tuningsystem\/kirnbergeriii"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningSystem"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Kirnberger III (Johan